hi guys welcome back and really glad to  make a youtube video today it's been a  long time I think the last video I made  was with Anthony my friend and there  wasn't proud a couple months ago we're  going to talk about that in a bit but  today I wanted to talk about fluency  what is fluency and I'm going to try to  make this not controversial but actually  useful for language learners now the  reason why I use the word controversial  is the because with the word fluency it  so much happens that a lot of people  debate quibble they say oh this is my  definition my definition is correct your  definition is wrong bla bla bla I think  that's really missing the forest for the  trees I think that there is no one fits  all size fits all definitional fluency  that the truth is that fluency is  something that should be defined by you  and if you define your own concept of  fluency the great thing that is going to  happen is that this is going to help you  actually carry out a an efficient  strategy it's really important in life  to have a precise goal and and this  helps you to define a strategy because  if you have a precise goal this defines  your action so without further ado I  would say that I'm going to give my own  definition of fluency so once again this  is my definition and my definition of  fluency is to be able to actually hold a  conversation to make it flow to  communicate smoothly fluently you know  the word fluent flow with other human  beings which actually implies two things  first that I can get my point across  even if I don't know all the words in  the language and the second thing is  that I can actually understand what is  being said to me now the interesting  thing is that a lot of people think that  fluency is some kind of final goal if  you're fluent you speak you understand  everything and you can say everything  but that is not exactly true let me give  an example I made a youtube video some  time ago maybe three years ago when I  was in Russia and I didn't remember the  word space combination or a mix actually  a mix of something and somebody wrote an  interesting comment which is not it's  not the only time  that comment like that was left under my  video as well as other videos saying  that if you don't know such an easy word  as a mix or mixture or whatever then  you're not fluent but the truth is I  thought well but just wait a second but  I was in rush I could speak I could  interact we talked about with a lot of  Russian Russians about philosophy  religion you name it and then the fact  that I didn't remember the word or  didn't remember I didn't even know the  word mix didn't hamper me from didn't  keep me hamper me from having  conversations and actually communicating  with people I think that in language  learning imagine learning a language  like making pizza you know it's there  are two main things that you have to do  you have to expand and you have to  refine so on the one hand you have this  piece of dough there and you put more  flour into it and the piece of dough  gets bigger but then if you don't refine  it if you don't give it a form then it's  going to be a formless big piece of  dough well if actually you refined you  have a piece of a piece of dough which  is not really big and you work on it you  will have a perfect piece of dough that  is too small so which means that in  terms of language learning it means that  if you learn too many words but you  don't learn how to put them together in  a given context in a conversation to  communicate with other human beings is  what is going to happen is that you know  a lot of words but you can't actually  communicate which is what happens all  the time for example to students who go  to to to school they know a lot of words  they know about the language but they  can't actually use it  this I call explicit knowledge and this  notion of explicit knowledge and  implicit knowledge you can find an  actually in an amazing book which I  can't find exactly right now but it's in  there and it's called Loudon it's a it's  a German book which talks about the fact  that you have explicit knowledge which  is know much about something in this  case about the language about grammar  rules and then actually the implicit  knowledge which is the ability to use  the language so to go back to the pizza  thing if you have a very small piece of  dough  then you have implicit not what you have  developed the capacity of using a few  pieces of information but that implies  that you can have you can rehearse your  kit you can be very good within certain  topics like for example you have you  have your own Islands you can say a lot  of things about a certain topic but if  you get out of your comfort zone or  somebody says something that you've  never heard or you're never talked about  then you get lost so the principle here  my strategy is actually to use implicit  implicit knowledge to develop implicit  knowledge which is the skill of  communicating with a relatively small  amount of words where a relatively small  means hundreds of words and so you build  we build or I build my knowledge upon  that using a few few words or the most  frequent words and I learn how to  communicate with human beings and then I  expand upon that because I still believe  that in order to speak a language well  and to know it well to be able to be  proficient in a language you have to  know a lot of words but proficiency and  fluency are two slightly different  concepts and my friend Anthony talks  about this in the article that he put  together and this article is going to  come out very very soon in a couple of  days I just wanted to anticipate this in  my video and it's going to be a really  cool article because it's not just about  talking it's not just talking about  fluency for the sake of talking about  fluency which leads to you know a lot of  discussions which probably they're not  very not going to be very useful but it  it gives you a very precise definition  of that and it gives you a very precise  strategy in things to do and tools to  use to finally communicate in a language  and fluently so if you want to check  that article you can check it I just put  the link down below on my blog which is  WWWE com I from now on I will try to  make us more videos because I've been I  haven't been very good with that due to  a lot of to a lot of things but you know  I always say that you always find the  time to do things if you want to do them  so I wish you a fantastic day and I will  talk to you very very soon bye
 

